11.0.0, twenty-third upload — the sound no longer clicks (exception build: crackle fix)

What is new since 10031. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds and tests; nothing
here is device-verified yet — the ear on the phone decides.
- The audio session asks for 48 kHz and a 512-frame buffer (10.7 ms), the values the earlier app
  used on devices; a refused request is written to the diagnostic log.
- Audio regions no longer click when Play starts inside a region, on a seek, on pause and play,
  or while Flow glides the tempo.
- Effect parameters and the synth's Character glide instead of stepping; throwing a parameter of
  any effect no longer clicks.
- The Harmonizer fades voices and style changes instead of switching them.
- The DDSP engine renders in time (it took far more than a core before; now about a quarter of
  one at 16 voices).
- A live output guard holds the master below -1 dBFS; exports are untouched.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10031), twenty-second upload — breath, float bakes, VoiceOver and large text.
10030 and earlier: see git history of this file.
group.com.echoelmusic is in the app's entitlements since a14e1960a (F17, 2026-10-21); the import
of earlier songs has not been seen on a device yet.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (FOUNDER_INBOX rule 1: five per build; answer each yes or no):
1. Play a song with an audio track and press Play in the middle of a region, then seek while it
   plays, then pause and play again. Any click?
2. Turn on the Harmonizer on a played line and switch its style while a voice sounds.
   Any click?
3. Play the synth with Character moving and throw an effect parameter (Chorus, EQ, Delay) fast.
   Any click or crackle?
4. Switch the synth to the DDSP engine and hold a chord of many notes. Does it play clean, with no
   dropouts?
5. Plug headphones in and out while playing. Does the sound carry on without a crack?
